# UI Unification Rules

## Objective
Keep client and admin visual systems consistent while preserving their functional differences.

## Shared design language

Both applications must use the same:

- color palette
- typography scale
- spacing scale
- radius scale
- shadow language
- icon style
- component naming conventions

## Differences allowed

- client UI may be denser in interaction
- admin UI may be denser in information
- layout structure may differ by usage scenario

## Requirement

All visual tokens must be defined once and shared across both ends.

## Forbidden

- introducing a second design language
- hardcoding unrelated colors in isolated components
- mixing incompatible layout conventions
